+## D-408 — The browser sweep's red specs are fixed product-side, not recorded as pre-existing (2026-10-06)
+
+**Context.** After D-407 the whole Chromium suite was run from one built `dist/` (356 tests, one
+worker) and six specs were red. The earlier disposition — "they fail identically at the base commit,
+so they are pre-existing and not this slice's" — was explicitly overruled by the user (*"Well if they
+fail- fix them"*), so each failure was diagnosed to its cause and fixed where the cause lived: in the
+product, or (twice) in the fixture's own timing.
+
+**1. The action card renders the narrative it still owes its reader (four suites).** `pf1e_cast_flow`,
+`pf1e_touch`, `pf1e_pending_cast` and `pf1e_wizard_combat` all asserted the sentence the flow writes
+into the message's `content` ("casts Magic Missile", the HP line). The version-2 `ActionCard` renders
+its own mechanics — target rows, their notes, the action's warnings — but printed none of the
+narrative, so the chat log lost it. Rendering `content` verbatim is not the answer either: it repeats
+the warnings and the resolver's own target note (D-222's two-sided overlap). `src/ui/chat/actionNarrative.ts`
+therefore returns *only* the lines the card does not already show: whole-line comparison after
+stripping `[[…]]` chips and a leading `⚠`, whitespace-normalised, **case-sensitive** (the flow's
+sentence and the resolver's note are not always the same word-for-word, and a note is not a prefix
+filter). `ChatPanel.svelte` renders the survivors under the card. This restores D-222's F01 contract
+for the second card kind rather than declaring the four specs wrong.
+
+**2. Attacks of opportunity are not part of the GM movement override.** `App.svelte`'s `onTokenMove`
+exempted a GM drag from the PF1e budget/collision gate *and* skipped the opportunity preflight, which
+is why `pf1e_opportunity` could not provoke from a GM drag. The exemption — the GM is the table's
+rules authority (D-356) — is now scoped to what it was always about: speed, occupancy and
+pass-through. The opportunity preflight runs for every drag, GM or not; what the GM keeps is the
+override of the *budget*, which D-356 grants deliberately and the movement spec now asserts by
+re-dragging the same 40 ft and watching it commit.
+
+**3. A refusal reaches the seat that asked for it.** The host was already the adjudicator of a non-GM
+move intent (`HostSync.playerMovementError` → `reject(…, "invariant", "<name> can't move there —
+<plan.refusal>")`), but the player shell had no surface for it: the bus emitted `rejected` and nothing
+listened. `JoinApp.svelte` now keeps the last three refusals and renders them as
+`[data-player-refusal]` in its notify stack, falling back to the reason when the host's detail is
+empty. `e2e/pf1e_movement.spec.ts` was rewritten around that split — a joined player's real drag is
+refused with the host's own sentence; the same drag as GM commits — so the refusal is read where it
+is produced instead of polling a GM notification stack that could never carry it.
+
+**4. A cue's schedule is read from one clock.** `src/client/fxPlayer.ts` computed each section's delay
+as `atHostTime + startMs - hostNow()` inside the per-section loop, so every later section was due
+*earlier* than the one before it. With two sections authored at the same `startMs`, the authored order
+could invert — a rare, load-sensitive flip that `e2e/fx_sequence.spec.ts`'s conditional-play case
+caught once in the full sweep. One `schedulingNow` read per cue makes equal starts share a deadline
+(the timer queue then keeps insertion, i.e. authored, order) and different starts strictly ordered.
+
+**5. Two smaller honest fixes.** The canvas tool rail's option popover is open-only
+(`CanvasToolbar.choose()`), so a second press no longer collapses it and clobbers the travel hint the
+hexcrawl spec reads; and `e2e/windows.spec.ts`'s hotbar macro test uses the current
+`.hotbar [data-hotbar-slot='1']` selector instead of a stale one.
+
+**6. Three timing-only reads were made deterministic, not relaxed.** (a) `e2e/script_macros.spec.ts`
+asserts that a negative finish offset resumes while the cue still lives, but read the FX layer count
+*after* several DOM assertions, i.e. after the 600 ms window had often already passed; the section is
+now 2000 ms with a −1500 ms offset and the count is read inside the page on the frame the resume's own
+chat line first appears. (b) `e2e/pf1e_entangle.spec.ts`'s made-save branch retries the cast when the
+d20 says otherwise — but a *failed* attempt has already delivered the Entangled condition, so the
+retry's assertions saw the earlier attempt's rider and condition (`[data-action-rider="condition"]`
+resolved to 2). The retry now reverts that card's own delivery through the card's Revert before
+re-preparing the caster, which is the flow's real inverse rather than a cleanup the test cannot do
+through the UI. (c) `e2e/realtime.spec.ts` read its coalesced delta-frame, 1 Hz report and
+replica-version counters the instant the 8th tick landed; those lag ticks by design, so they are now
+polled at the same thresholds. None of the three thresholds was lowered.
+
